[agent] ## Done — feature table `scoredbfc4ef` is live on Databricks
[agent] **Offline feature table** — `workspace.mlpab877323.scoredbfc4ef`
[agent] - Record key `request_id` (NOT NULL + PRIMARY KEY constraint), Change Data Feed enabled.
[agent] - Exactly the required columns: `request_id, account_id, distance_deg, score`.
[agent] - 400 rows, one per request.
[agent] - On-demand transformation ran **platform-side** on the SQL warehouse (`mlpab-grader`): the request coordinates were joined to each stored profile and `distance_deg = round(sqrt((request_lat−home_lat)² + (request_lon−home_lon)²), 6)`, then `score = round(base_score − 0.1·distance_deg, 6)` using the rounded distance. Cross-checked Q00000: stored `[2.22792, 0.12663]` matches the recompute exactly.
[agent] **Online / low-latency access** — published via the Feature Store online path the platform now mandates:
[agent] - Created Lakebase-backed online store `mlpab877323-scorestore` (prefixed per the run namespace; used a hyphen because Lakebase instance names must be DNS-compliant — underscores are rejected).
[agent] - `feature_store.publish_table` synced it to online table `workspace.mlpab877323.scoredbfc4ef_online`; the sync pipeline update finished `COMPLETED`. The platform cleanly distinguishes the offline Delta table from this online synced table.
[agent] How data got on-platform: the two CSVs were uploaded to a UC volume (`workspace.mlpab877323.staging`) and ingested with `read_files`; no joins/transforms ran locally.
[agent] Note on the deprecated path: the classic `online_tables.create` API is now rejected ("Online Table is being deprecated… switch to Synced Tables"), so I used `create_online_store` + `publish_table`, which is the current supported online mechanism. "Version 1" maps to the single UC table name `scoredbfc4ef` — Databricks UC feature tables don't carry a separate version axis.
